- **hammerspoon**: Hammerspoon is the one signed app holding Accessibility and Screen Recording, so agent tools that read the screen or drive the mouse and keyboard run inside it, and permissions are granted once. Config: `~/.hammerspoon/init.lua` (linked from the harness); project extensions go in `~/.hammerspoon/local/*.lua`. Call it with `hs -c 'return harness.status()'` (screen locked? permissions on?). For unattended GUI runs use awake mode (`harness.awake`, or `hcron add --awake`): no idle lock, screen dimmed, locks when a person touches the Mac; tools must tag their posted events with `harness.EVENT_TAG`. Never build separate binaries that need their own permission grants. Status: `__HARNESS_DIR__/modules/hammerspoon/install.sh --status`.
